WEBVTT

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.190
She should have gone this way.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:07.930
Let's look over there.

00:00:12.130 --> 00:00:13.650
It seems they've left.

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.530
What did you do?

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:17.240
Yeah,

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.790
and why do you

00:00:18.790 --> 00:00:22.450
think I did something?

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:30.860
Serikyan!

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:32.460
Hey, don't say that so loud.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:34.220
You know her, Nanami?

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.430
You don't know Serikyan?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:39.640
She's an idol on the national stage...

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.100
Ginyuuin Serika!

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:42.880
Huh?

00:00:43.870 --> 00:00:45.550
Ginyuuin...

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:57.370
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.030
<b>Flag 11</b>

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:21.030
<b>We Don't all Have to Dance. I can Dance by Myself</b>

00:02:21.530 --> 00:02:24.890
She's sold more than 10,000,000 CDs!

00:02:24.890 --> 00:02:28.050
Her photos make magazines sell five times better!

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:30.210
She's constantly on tons 
of different TV programs.

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:34.610
In just the last six months she's 
climbed to the top of the rankings.

00:02:34.610 --> 00:02:37.000
She's easily the most famous idol right now.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.630
Her name: Serikyan!

00:02:39.630 --> 00:02:41.010
Sorry, I've never heard of her.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:43.010
Are you stupid?

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:44.240
You've never heard of Serikyan?!

00:02:44.240 --> 00:02:46.240
Do you come from another world
where they don't have TVs?

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.390
Do you live with the elves? Are you an elf?!

00:02:49.550 --> 00:02:51.810
I guess I need to work on my popularity.

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.280
No, it's fine, Serikyan.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:56.140
This guy's an elf and doesn't know anything.

00:02:56.140 --> 00:02:56.740
Wait...

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.830
Thanks for letting me borrow 
your uniform, Nanami-chin.

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:07.480
The uniforms are really cute.

00:03:08.340 --> 00:03:11.540
Serikyan in a school uniform is so great.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.590
Yes, if you use that uniform 
to disguise yourself,

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.740
it should be more difficult 
for people to recognize you.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:19.470
You know what you're doing, Nanami-chin!

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.470
I'll give you a hug.

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:25.490
I've never seen this side of Nanami.

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:28.350
I never would have thought 
you'd be so into idols.

00:03:29.150 --> 00:03:30.420
I don't like idols.

00:03:30.420 --> 00:03:31.770
I like Serikyan!

00:03:32.110 --> 00:03:34.960
So why is this "Serikyan" here anyway?

00:03:35.260 --> 00:03:37.660
You don't know anything, do you?

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.270
On the last day of the School Fair,

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:40.990
there's a special Serikyan concert.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:42.300
That's obviously why she's here.

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.040
Wait...

00:03:43.340 --> 00:03:45.280
Today isn't the last day.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:48.410
Well, I wanted to take a 
look at the stage and such,

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:51.790
and you know, have some 
fun at the fair, maybe.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:55.710
Well, then, we'll just have to 
show you around the fair, then!

00:03:55.950 --> 00:03:57.790
Thank you, Nanami-chin!

00:03:58.090 --> 00:04:00.340
But aren't you on a date with your boyfriend?

00:04:00.760 --> 00:04:02.480
H-He's not my boyfriend.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:04.300
You're far more important to me

00:04:04.300 --> 00:04:06.690
than this dark elf over here.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:09.200
Now, let's go.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:11.140
Sure!

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:19.100
The bard from the fairy tale...

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.960
I imagine that's her...

00:04:24.110 --> 00:04:25.880
<i>No use in worrying about it.</i>

00:04:25.880 --> 00:04:27.980
<i>I decided that I would have fun while I can.</i>

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:30.120
What are you doing?

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:32.020
Hurry up.

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.410
R-Right.

00:04:53.890 --> 00:04:55.140
President!

00:05:02.430 --> 00:05:04.100
I can't believe you.

00:05:04.100 --> 00:05:08.100
How many girls are you leading on?

00:05:08.100 --> 00:05:10.280
I'm not really...

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:13.470
You were supposed to be on a date 
at the school fair with Nanami-chin,

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:15.250
but now you're flirting 
with other girls instead.

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:17.750
I feel bad for Nanami-chin!

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:21.440
It wasn't a date. 
It was more like I forced him,

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:24.550
but I'm glad you're concerned for me!

00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:26.090
Serikyan!

00:05:26.090 --> 00:05:27.590
Nanami-chin!

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:30.530
Uh...

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:30.930
Hm?

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.920
You wanted to see the stage you'll be 
performing on during the last day, right?

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:36.440
I think that's it.

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:49.780
You're a national idol,

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:52.020
so this might not be much,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:54.790
but we're all looking forward 
to your performance.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:59.290
No, I like these local concerts.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.470
The first concert I performed 
was at a school fair.

00:06:03.280 --> 00:06:06.160
A school fair at my middle school...

00:06:06.160 --> 00:06:07.960
We didn't have a stage,

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:10.760
so we just decorated the gym.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.470
<b>Ginyuuin Serika Idol Debut</b>

00:06:13.700 --> 00:06:16.470
I had just debuted,

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.250
and couldn't sing because I was so nervous.

00:06:19.670 --> 00:06:21.730
But my classmates

00:06:22.190 --> 00:06:25.190
and my teachers cheered me on.

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.090
I was so happy I could've cried.

00:06:27.390 --> 00:06:29.570
They supported me.

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:31.740
But...

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.240
For the next year and a half 
no one even noticed me.

00:06:35.860 --> 00:06:38.750
I was an idol in name only.

00:06:41.420 --> 00:06:42.430
Talent.

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:44.410
I guess I don't have any.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.850
Maybe I should stop calling myself an idol.

00:06:52.050 --> 00:06:54.580
I'm supposed to make everyone happy,

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.590
but instead they made me feel happy,

00:06:57.590 --> 00:06:59.260
and I couldn't even return the favor...

00:07:00.080 --> 00:07:03.230
I wish I could do more...

00:07:03.660 --> 00:07:04.520
I...

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.540
You can't give up here.

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:23.470
Huh?

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:27.140
You will come to inspire people,

00:07:27.460 --> 00:07:30.150
and become a woman that 
represents people's dreams.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:32.730
Your heart is not yet dead.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:35.730
If you fall, you can get back up,

00:07:35.730 --> 00:07:37.660
provided you don't give up.

00:07:39.950 --> 00:07:42.560
I can keep going?

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.720
Do you think I can fly again?

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:48.690
Do you think I can sing and give people hope?

00:07:49.670 --> 00:07:50.440
You can.

00:07:55.490 --> 00:07:56.920
You have a flag on

00:07:57.220 --> 00:08:00.130
your head that says you'll succeed.

00:08:05.220 --> 00:08:06.880
I'll do it!

00:08:10.370 --> 00:08:12.020
Half a year later,

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:15.660
Serikyan became a super-idol,

00:08:15.660 --> 00:08:17.510
and it was all thanks to his words.

00:08:17.910 --> 00:08:19.860
He said I had a success flag.

00:08:19.860 --> 00:08:21.180
What a prophet.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:25.060
I call him the purple flag guy.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:27.730
I never was able to thank him,

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:29.430
but I wonder if he's out there somewhere,

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:31.050
having heard my songs.

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.740
I guess I just told you

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.710
my secret origin story. Whoops.

00:08:36.710 --> 00:08:38.060
Don't tell anyone,

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:41.540
'Kay? 'Kay?

00:08:41.800 --> 00:08:43.370
R-Right.

00:08:43.800 --> 00:08:45.970
Anyway, I'll be going.

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:48.280
You're leaving, Serikyan?

00:08:48.280 --> 00:08:51.090
Serikyan leaves, you know?!

00:08:51.090 --> 00:08:52.050
What are you saying...

00:08:52.270 --> 00:08:55.050
I'm glad I ran into you Nanami-chin!

00:08:55.050 --> 00:08:57.990
Come to my concert!

00:08:57.990 --> 00:09:01.220
I guess you can come, too, Hatate.

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:03.120
Anyway, bye.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:08.980
Hey, Hatate Souta-kun.

00:09:09.390 --> 00:09:11.280
What is it, Nanami-san?

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:13.130
It could just be me,

00:09:13.130 --> 00:09:16.780
but I think I have an idea 
who this purple flag guy is.

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.120
It's probably just you.

00:09:19.780 --> 00:09:21.810
Yeah, I guess it is.

00:09:21.810 --> 00:09:23.580
Silly me.

00:09:23.580 --> 00:09:25.460
Silly Nanami.

00:09:27.170 --> 00:09:29.890
Is there anyone else who'd go off

00:09:29.890 --> 00:09:32.290
about flags when no one wanted them to?!

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:34.190
I had a lot of stuff

00:09:34.190 --> 00:09:36.680
going on back then, so...

00:09:38.050 --> 00:09:39.360
When I saw her

00:09:40.630 --> 00:09:43.180
I was planning on taking

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:44.960
my own life.

00:09:50.330 --> 00:09:51.520
I guess

00:09:52.210 --> 00:09:54.880
I wanted to do one good thing before I died.

00:09:55.370 --> 00:09:58.280
Ultimately, I couldn't end it all, though.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:03.040
I guess it was pretty tough for you.

00:10:03.260 --> 00:10:06.850
So I wasn't really thinking 
about her specifically, per se.

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:08.950
I was just trying to make myself feel better.

00:10:08.950 --> 00:10:11.490
Yeah, but you still helped her.

00:10:11.490 --> 00:10:13.410
You saved her, right?

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:14.130
Huh?

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.390
Serikyan recovered,

00:10:16.390 --> 00:10:18.350
I got to know you...

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:20.330
Everyone was happy in the end.

00:10:20.700 --> 00:10:24.530
You know, if you'd used your power like this from the start,

00:10:24.530 --> 00:10:26.020
you wouldn't have had such a hard time.

00:10:26.450 --> 00:10:27.520
Nanami...

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.710
Anyway, putting that aside...

00:10:30.710 --> 00:10:31.360
Huh?

00:10:32.390 --> 00:10:35.040
It pisses me off that Serikyan

00:10:35.040 --> 00:10:37.530
owes you so much!

00:10:36.480 --> 00:10:37.530
Wai—

00:10:37.530 --> 00:10:40.470
Making your way into 
Serikyan's heart like that!

00:10:40.470 --> 00:10:41.300
You're acting crazy.

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:42.930
They're fighting.

00:10:42.930 --> 00:10:44.320
First time I've seen something like this.

00:10:52.280 --> 00:10:54.380
Everyone, it's time!

00:10:54.670 --> 00:10:56.910
It's finally the last day of the fair.

00:10:56.910 --> 00:11:00.300
It's time for the grand finale!

00:11:00.670 --> 00:11:02.800
Yes, the time has come!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:06.310
Akane's got new clothes and 
totally is ready to go.

00:11:06.570 --> 00:11:09.370
Way to go, Akane, but I've

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:12.750
mastered a new dance!

00:11:12.750 --> 00:11:15.360
Sounds like you're excited, too!

00:11:15.660 --> 00:11:17.800
The night dance party!

00:11:15.810 --> 00:11:17.500
Serikyan's concert!

00:11:17.800 --> 00:11:18.570
Huh?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:28.000
Ta-da!

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:32.750
Sob. Sob.

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.040
H-How are we, Souta?

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:37.340
Don't just stand there. Say something.

00:11:37.340 --> 00:11:39.010
Huh? Y-Yeah...

00:11:41.720 --> 00:11:44.180
You all look great.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:47.120
Yeah, we all tried hard for you.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:49.190
Yes, we can't embarrass ourselves

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.350
when we dance with you.

00:11:51.350 --> 00:11:53.400
Huh? With me?

00:11:54.850 --> 00:11:57.650
Everyone wants to dance with you.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:02.090
There's a legend regarding this dance party.

00:12:02.090 --> 00:12:03.160
Legend?

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:05.860
It'd be nice if the couples that

00:12:05.860 --> 00:12:08.040
dance get married in the future.

00:12:08.550 --> 00:12:10.020
Nice? That's all?

00:12:10.020 --> 00:12:13.120
Must be nice to be a guy.

00:12:13.120 --> 00:12:16.670
As your little sister, I don't 
mind how many step-sisters I get.

00:12:17.350 --> 00:12:18.800
You can't say that.

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:22.140
My little brother should 
only have one older sister!

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:23.810
That doesn't even make any sense.

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.960
It's nice being this old.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:28.600
I get to feel like I'm dancing with my grandson.

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:31.010
H-Hatate-kun,

00:12:31.010 --> 00:12:34.560
could you dance with me, too?

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:36.780
I can't dance.

00:12:36.780 --> 00:12:39.610
I'll lead for you, I will.

00:12:39.610 --> 00:12:42.050
Everyone wants to dance with you.

00:12:42.050 --> 00:12:44.500
Everyone really wants to.

00:12:44.500 --> 00:12:46.700
Will you dance with us?!

00:12:48.700 --> 00:12:50.720
<i>Dance partner flags...</i>

00:12:52.370 --> 00:12:53.570
Got it.

00:12:53.570 --> 00:12:54.960
I'm not confident at all,

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:56.210
but let's dance.

00:12:56.210 --> 00:12:57.710
Yay!

00:12:57.930 --> 00:13:00.090
In that case it's a promise!

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:01.910
Yeah, promise.

00:13:06.170 --> 00:13:10.430
I-I'm fine with seeing Serikyan's 
concert alone, but...

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:11.390
But...

00:13:11.990 --> 00:13:15.450
If you're the only one not dancing 
it'll feel like you're left out,

00:13:15.450 --> 00:13:16.100
right?

00:13:16.100 --> 00:13:19.770
D-Don't say it before I do!

00:13:43.380 --> 00:13:45.630
Serikyan!

00:13:45.910 --> 00:13:49.150
Thank you all for coming to

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:50.890
Serikyan's school concert!

00:13:52.040 --> 00:13:54.140
Are you having fun at the fair?

00:13:54.400 --> 00:13:56.850
I actually secretly went around

00:13:56.850 --> 00:13:59.060
the fair with some friends.

00:13:59.060 --> 00:14:00.890
It was a lot of fun!

00:14:00.890 --> 00:14:03.650
I totally love this school now!

00:14:03.650 --> 00:14:05.510
Serikyan!

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:09.810
Today's concert will be broadcast

00:14:09.810 --> 00:14:11.870
to fans all around the world!

00:14:11.870 --> 00:14:15.410
So cheer appropriately.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:20.840
Nanami-chan broke.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:23.610
But I'm kind of having fun.

00:14:23.610 --> 00:14:25.920
I want to shout with everyone.

00:14:26.190 --> 00:14:28.140
Broadcast all around the world. huh?

00:14:28.140 --> 00:14:29.430
Pretty amazing.

00:14:31.360 --> 00:14:32.940
She really made it.

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:35.030
She turned into a girl who inspires people,

00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:38.100
who represents their dreams.

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:40.600
I found Nanami-chin.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:43.860
I see that Hatate came, too.

00:14:44.770 --> 00:14:45.610
<i>Huh?</i>

00:14:51.080 --> 00:14:53.780
Listen to my song!

00:14:54.040 --> 00:14:58.440
<i>I saw you yesterday, 
but will I see you again today?</i>

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:02.600
<i>My biorhythm is focused on you.</i>

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.000
<i>We only could talk for a 
bit, but I still got red.</i>

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:11.300
<i>I'm such a girl.</i>

00:15:11.300 --> 00:15:13.100
<i>As the gelato melts,</i>

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:15.600
<i>as the candy melts...</i>

00:15:16.680 --> 00:15:18.850
<i>What's that?</i>

00:15:21.910 --> 00:15:24.160
<i>A flag of light?</i>

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:35.160
<i>Could this be...</i>

00:15:35.880 --> 00:15:38.800
<i>Did my power get stronger when I met</i>

00:15:39.030 --> 00:15:41.850
<i>Serika, the bard?</i>

00:15:42.890 --> 00:15:44.420
<i>No, this light is...</i>

00:15:48.110 --> 00:15:49.400
<i>They're connected.</i>

00:15:49.700 --> 00:15:53.220
<i>The world is being drawn 
to her flag and song.</i>

00:15:58.330 --> 00:15:59.340
<i>It's being drawn to me?</i>

00:16:06.390 --> 00:16:08.000
<i>So that's how it is..</i>

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:11.820
<i>I thought that my death flag drew 
evil from all over the world,</i>

00:16:12.380 --> 00:16:15.950
<i>and brought me nothing but despair.</i>

00:16:16.340 --> 00:16:17.330
<i>But that was wrong.</i>

00:16:18.180 --> 00:16:20.190
<i>I have people connected to me with</i>

00:16:20.510 --> 00:16:22.620
<i>kindness that can overcome any evil.</i>

00:16:23.430 --> 00:16:25.830
<i>I have people who give me hope 
that will paint over the despair.</i>

00:16:26.440 --> 00:16:28.800
<i>All I did was turn my back on the world,</i>

00:16:29.400 --> 00:16:31.800
<i>so I didn't notice something so simple.</i>

00:16:40.650 --> 00:16:41.600
<i>Nanami...</i>

00:16:41.600 --> 00:16:42.580
<i>Akane...</i>

00:16:42.880 --> 00:16:43.560
<i>Okiku-nee...</i>

00:16:44.300 --> 00:16:45.360
<i>Everyone...</i>

00:16:47.520 --> 00:16:48.570
Hatate Souta.

00:16:51.810 --> 00:16:52.710
You're...

00:16:53.800 --> 00:16:55.410
Number Zero.

00:16:57.940 --> 00:16:59.540
What are these numbers?

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.380
I guess other data than the 
flags has become visible.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:07.450
The sudden growth of that power of 
yours strained the servers,

00:17:07.450 --> 00:17:09.550
and the world froze.

00:17:10.040 --> 00:17:11.260
What are you saying—

00:17:13.050 --> 00:17:14.990
The parallel world I went to with Mei.

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:18.570
The term "virtual world" would be more apt.

00:17:18.810 --> 00:17:19.670
Virtual?

00:17:20.050 --> 00:17:23.000
This is one of the many worlds we,

00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.850
the Council of the Seven Virtues,

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:27.310
created to help combat the Angel Boat.

00:17:27.970 --> 00:17:29.780
An existence in the network.

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.570
A world composed of data.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:36.650
The trouble began when

00:17:36.650 --> 00:17:39.250
the system that exists in 
cyberspace to watch over

00:17:39.250 --> 00:17:41.840
the real world, the Angel 
Boat, went out of control.

00:17:41.840 --> 00:17:45.290
At this rate, it's only a matter 
of time before humanity,

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:47.830
which depends so much on the network, 
is controlled by computers.

00:17:48.310 --> 00:17:50.320
In order to prevent that, we—

00:17:52.870 --> 00:17:54.830
You seem rather calm.

00:17:55.570 --> 00:17:58.050
I'd like to scream 
and say you're lying,

00:17:58.780 --> 00:18:00.930
but the truth flag above your head,

00:18:01.530 --> 00:18:03.530
and everything I see here...

00:18:03.850 --> 00:18:07.380
Yes, your power is needed for the world.

00:18:07.680 --> 00:18:09.340
You can see the flags and control them.

00:18:09.340 --> 00:18:12.700
Only that power of yours that 
can alter the data of all events

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:16.020
can reach the Angel Boat in cyberspace.

00:18:16.020 --> 00:18:17.740
It is the best and only weapon we have.

00:18:19.470 --> 00:18:21.010
Yeah, I know,

00:18:21.540 --> 00:18:23.530
or more like I know everything now.

00:18:24.010 --> 00:18:25.870
I just gained all the

00:18:26.960 --> 00:18:29.120
information on the network.

00:18:31.360 --> 00:18:34.320
But there is one thing I don't understand.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:36.130
Why me?

00:18:36.540 --> 00:18:38.350
We, the Council of the Seven Virtues,

00:18:38.350 --> 00:18:41.710
have been running simulations 
in the worlds we created

00:18:41.710 --> 00:18:43.650
with the data from all humanity.

00:18:43.650 --> 00:18:46.030
We set the simulations to run

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:48.440
one hundred million times

00:18:48.440 --> 00:18:50.940
faster than reality.

00:18:51.590 --> 00:18:55.440
The Sacrament guided our way.

00:18:56.790 --> 00:18:58.380
You know the rest.

00:18:59.040 --> 00:19:01.100
The Hatate Souta of this world...

00:19:01.400 --> 00:19:03.920
In other words, only you have met with

00:19:03.920 --> 00:19:05.740
the Sacrament and been given power.

00:19:06.570 --> 00:19:08.410
Is this a coincidence?

00:19:08.410 --> 00:19:10.730
Or an inevitability by the name of fate?

00:19:10.730 --> 00:19:12.560
That is up to you.

00:19:13.030 --> 00:19:15.290
What is Sakura...

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:17.190
No, the Sacrament.

00:19:17.570 --> 00:19:19.120
It doesn't really matter,

00:19:19.420 --> 00:19:21.380
now that your power has grown,

00:19:21.380 --> 00:19:23.700
and been perfected.

00:19:25.340 --> 00:19:26.200
<i>Sakura...</i>

00:19:28.450 --> 00:19:30.240
<i>I understand everything now.</i>

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:34.410
<i>Even I can't break this death flag of mine.</i>

00:19:34.790 --> 00:19:35.770
<i>It's a curse.</i>

00:19:36.480 --> 00:19:38.670
<i>You gave me this power</i>

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:40.710
<i>so I'd understand that?</i>

00:19:41.200 --> 00:19:44.470
Now, what will you do with 
that power, Hatate Souta?

00:19:45.050 --> 00:19:47.020
What will happen to this world now?

00:19:47.580 --> 00:19:49.900
Now that your power has been perfected,

00:19:49.900 --> 00:19:52.060
it won't end with a simple freeze next time.

00:19:52.360 --> 00:19:54.390
I imagine it'll completely collapse,

00:19:55.220 --> 00:19:57.310
so long as you are here.

00:19:58.560 --> 00:19:59.560
I see.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:04.800
I... can't be here anymore, I guess.

00:20:18.230 --> 00:20:24.490
<b>Dance Party</b>

00:20:18.620 --> 00:20:21.500
It's time for the Hatagaya 
School Fair to end!

00:20:21.500 --> 00:20:23.340
Good work, everyone!

00:20:24.770 --> 00:20:27.660
The only thing left is the dance party!

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:29.080
Everyone dance

00:20:29.080 --> 00:20:32.160
<i>your hearts out!</i>

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.450
This is only one of the many virtual worlds.

00:20:41.510 --> 00:20:45.270
But... it was the only world I had.

00:20:46.770 --> 00:20:50.770
What is Souta off doing?

00:20:50.770 --> 00:20:52.220
It's fine.

00:20:52.220 --> 00:20:56.020
He promised he'd dance with everyone.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.030
I'm sorry, everyone.

00:20:59.700 --> 00:21:01.660
I'm sorry, Nee-san.

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:06.850
What was that feeling just now?

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:09.840
Is something wrong, Nanami-chan?

00:21:09.840 --> 00:21:11.750
It's nothing.

00:21:11.970 --> 00:21:15.480
Everything's going to be over soon.

00:21:15.480 --> 00:21:17.750
I wonder what Souta's doing.

00:21:20.250 --> 00:21:21.380
Uh...

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:25.340
Who's Souta-kun?

00:21:26.670 --> 00:21:27.320
Huh?

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:12.660
Roar! Gawo!

00:23:14.030 --> 00:23:15.450
I wonder what I'm saying.

00:23:16.130 --> 00:23:19.390
I'm thinking about that place, 
all of them, before I realize it.

00:23:19.790 --> 00:23:23.920
I'm sure that's because 
I was happy until today.

00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:27.760
That's why I might not be able to go back.

00:23:28.050 --> 00:23:30.200
But as long as everyone's smiling back there,

00:23:30.510 --> 00:23:32.200
no matter what flags I have to break,

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>Flag 12</b>

00:23:31.010 --> 00:23:35.010
<b>It's a Cruel World. I'm Going to Take a Look in the Shadows.</b>

00:23:32.570 --> 00:23:33.650
I'll protect them.

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>If Her Flag Breaks</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>You'd better watch next time!</b>

00:23:35.010 --> 00:23:40.020
Illustration: Aoki Ume
